{
 "encounter_id": "00952",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
  "person_4": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "Dr Hughes, this is Arlo, he's five, and his mum is here about his snoring. I'll leave you to it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thanks, nurse. Hello Arlo, hello Mum. What's been going on? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He snores. Properly, like a lorry. It's been about a year, getting worse."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I don't snore. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "You do, sweetheart. I recorded it, I've got it on my phone. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Could I hear a bit of it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Of course. Here you go. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Goodness. That's loud. Does he stop breathing at all, in the night?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Sometimes it sounds like he pauses. Not for long. A few seconds."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does he have a fever at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No fever, no."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any trouble swallowing?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "None, he eats like a horse."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And during the day, how's he? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "A bit cranky by the afternoon. He used to nap, and he doesn't now. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And does he ever wake up grumpy or tired? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Yes, he's often grumpy first thing. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is there a history of tonsil problems, Mum?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He's had tonsillitis twice, last year."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Where's he at in school?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Reception, at the village primary."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Arlo, can you open your mouth wide like a lion? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Roar! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Perfect. Can you do it again? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Roar! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, I can see. Mum, I'm going to explain what I'm looking for. Tonsils sit at the back of the throat. In some children, they are very big. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Are his big? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll tell you after I've explained what the options are. Sometimes big tonsils can narrow the airway at night. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is that what's causing the snoring? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It might be. I won't put a label on it today. I'd like to arrange an overnight oxygen level test at home, so we can see how he breathes while he sleeps."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "How does that work? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A small sensor goes on his toe, and it records through the night. The nurse will give you the kit. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "I'll get it ready for you, Mrs Webb. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "And then? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Then we'll know whether it's a simple snore or whether it affects his sleep. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "That makes sense. Thank you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Arlo, you were a very good lion. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Rrrr! ~"
  }
